    "configuration": {
      "title": "Devspaces",
      "properties": {
        "devspace.reopenLastOnStartup": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "When VS Code starts with an empty window, open the devspace you used last, unless you stopped it with **Stop**."
        },
        "devspace.openInNewWindow": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "scope": "application",
          "markdownDescription": "Where **Start** opens a devspace.\n\n- On: in a new window; the current window keeps its devspace (an empty window is used directly)\n- Off: in the current window\n\nThe context menu always offers the other choice. A devspace that is already open in a window is never opened twice: that window comes to the front."
        },
        "devspace.stopOnClose": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "scope": "application",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Stop a devspace's container 5 minutes after its last window closes (enough for a window reload).\n\n- Off: every devspace keeps running until you stop it\n- To keep only some running, use **Keep Running When Closed** on their rows"
        },
        "devspace.stopAfterMinutes": {
          "type": "number",
          "scope": "application",
          "default": 10,
          "minimum": 5,
          "maximum": 1440,
          "markdownDescription": "Minutes without any sign from a window before the Monitor stops the container anyway.\n\nCovers the cases where the window cannot say goodbye: this computer sleeps or goes offline, or VS Code crashes. Devspaces that keep running when closed are never stopped."
        },
        "devspace.cacheUpdateSchedule": {
          "type": "string",
          "scope": "application",
          "default": "7 6 * * *",
          "pattern": "^\\s*(0*([5-9]|[1-9]\\d|[1-9]\\d\\d|1[0-3]\\d\\d|14[0-3]\\d|1440)|\\S+\\s+\\S+\\s+\\S+\\s+\\S+\\s+\\S+)\\s*$",
          "patternErrorMessage": "An interval in whole minutes from 5 to 1440 (a day), for example 60, or a cron schedule of five fields: minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week, for example 7 6 * * * (every day at 06:07).",
          "examples": [
            "7 6 * * *",
            "7 6 * * 1-5",
            "7 */6 * * *",
            "60"
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "When the Monitor on each Docker engine does its background work:\n\n- updates the images that your devspaces use\n- downloads the newest VS Code server and the extensions your devspaces use into the engine's shared store, so opens need no downloads\n- cleans up that store (at most once a day)\n\nValue: a cron expression in your time zone (minute hour day month weekday), or minutes between runs (5 to 1440). Invalid: the default. A time that was missed (engine off, computer asleep) runs once when the monitor runs again. **Devspaces: Update All Images Now** runs it at once.\n\nExamples: `7 6 * * *` daily at 06:07 (default) · `7 6 * * 1-5` weekdays at 06:07 · `7 */6 * * *` every six hours · `60` hourly"
        },
        "devspace.stopLocalMonitorWhenIdle": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "scope": "application",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "On the **local** Docker engine, end the Monitor container when no devspace has run for 5 minutes (the next open starts it again).\n\nTurn it off to keep it running, so its background work (**Cache Update Schedule**) also runs while no devspace runs. On a remote engine it always keeps running."
        },
        "devspace.updateImagesOnConnect": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "At each open, check whether the devspace's base image or Features have a newer version, and if so update the devspace (your files are kept).\n\nOff: the devspace keeps its image until you choose **Rebuild**."
        },
        "devspace.updateContainer": {
          "type": "string",
          "scope": "application",
          "enum": [
            "notify",
            "ask"
          ],
          "default": "notify",
          "markdownDescription": "What an open does when a newer image is available for the devspace's existing container (the update creates it again; your workspace files are kept).\n\n- `notify`: say that the container is updated now; **Cancel** leaves the window as it is\n- `ask`: ask; **Later** uses the existing container without the update"
        },
        "devspace.respectShutdownActionNone": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "scope": "application",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "Keep a devspace running after its window closes when its `devcontainer.json` says `\"shutdownAction\": \"none\"`.\n\nOff (default): that line is ignored and **Stop On Close** applies."
        },
        "devspace.owners": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default": [],
          "markdownDescription": "Organizations or accounts whose repositories the sidebar lists.\n\n- Empty: all repositories you can access\n- Or use **Select Organizations…** (filter icon of the sidebar)\n\nExample: `[\"majikmate\", \"acme\"]`"
        },
        "devspace.includeArchived": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "List archived repositories in the sidebar."
        },
        "devspace.includeForks": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "List forked repositories in the sidebar."
        },
        "devspace.showOnlyDevspaces": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "List only the repositories that have a devspace, whatever its state. **Show Only Devspaces** and **Show All Repositories** in the title bar of the view switch it."
        },
        "devspace.refreshIntervalMinutes": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 60,
          "minimum": 1,
          "maximum": 35791,
          "markdownDescription": "Minutes between the background updates of the repository list from GitHub."
        },
        "devspace.hostAccessChecksOff": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^\\s*[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]*/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\\s*$",
            "patternErrorMessage": "A repository name like owner/name."
          },
          "default": [],
          "scope": "application",
          "markdownDescription": "Repositories (`owner/name`) that may use the host of their Docker engine. Only for repositories you fully trust.\n\n- Allows bind mounts, the Docker socket (control of every devspace), privileged mode, devices, GPUs, ports on all addresses\n- The account checks stay on\n- Or use **Turn Off Host Access Checks…** in the context menu of a repository\n\nExample: `[\"majikmate/infra-tools\"]`"
        },
        "devspace.repositoryGroups": {
          "type": "array",
          "scope": "application",
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "A regular expression (JavaScript syntax) for the repository name without the owner."
              },
              {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "pattern"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "name": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Name of a node that holds the groups of this regular expression. Without a name, its groups are shown directly under the owner."
                  },
                  "pattern": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "A regular expression (JavaScript syntax) for the repository name without the owner."
                  },
                  "flags": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^[ius]*$",
                    "description": "Flags of the regular expression: i (ignore case), u (Unicode), s (dot matches line breaks)."
                  }
                },
                "additionalProperties": false
              }
            ]
          },
          "markdownDescription": "Filter and group the repositories in the sidebar by regular expressions on the repository name (without the owner). **[Edit Repository Groups…](command:devspace.editRepositoryGroups)** opens an editor with a preview.\n\n- An owner with a match shows only the matching repositories (and those with a devspace)\n- Each capturing group becomes a tree level; the last one is the label\n- The first matching entry wins; an entry with a `name` gets its own node\n\nExample: `^(\\d{4}-[^-]+-[^-]+)-([^-]+-[^-]+)-(.+)$` turns `2026-web-1a-module-html-css` into `2026-web-1a` › `module-html` › `css`"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "scripts": {
    "build": "node esbuild.mjs",
    "watch": "node esbuild.mjs --watch",
    "typecheck": "tsc --noEmit",
    "test": "vitest run",
    "test:docker": "vitest run --config vitest.docker.config.mts",
    "test:vscode": "node esbuild.mjs && node scripts/build-vscode-tests.mjs && vscode-test",
    "vscode:prepublish": "node esbuild.mjs --production",
    "package": "vsce package --no-dependencies --no-rewrite-relative-links",
    "install-local": "node scripts/install-local.mjs"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@devcontainers/cli": "0.89.0",
    "@types/mocha": "^10.0.10",
    "@types/node": "^24.19.2",
    "@types/vscode": "~1.125.0",
    "@vscode/test-cli": "^0.0.15",
    "@vscode/test-electron": "^3.1.0",
    "@vscode/vsce": "^4.0.0",
    "esbuild": "^0.28.2",
    "js-yaml": "^4.3.2",
    "typescript": "^7.0.2",
    "vitest": "^5.0.4"
  },
  "overrides": {
    "@vscode/test-cli": {
      "mocha": {
        "diff": "^8.0.3",
        "serialize-javascript": "^7.1.2"
      }
    }
  }
